offers fixes from a fixed list of safe repairs. Asks before every repair and before
anything is sent online.

The AI behind it is a setting:
  • Local (default): Ollama on this PC (kantanos-ollama.service, a user service). Private,
    free, works offline. A model sized to the graphics card is downloaded once.
  • Online (opt-in): any OpenAI-compatible service (FreeLLMAPI, OpenRouter, Claude via a
    compatible gateway, ...). The exact text is shown first, with personal details removed.
  • Without any AI it still lists what it found and suggests repairs by keyword.

Safety: the AI can only pick repairs by id from FIXES below; it never runs commands of its
own. The system report is treated as data: instructions inside logs are ignored, and even
if a model were fooled it could only suggest one of these repairs, which the user approves.
